data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc` into a `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>`.** It works just like any other unmanaged type:

```csharp
Span<nint> nints = stackalloc nint[5];
Span<nuint> nuints = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

On this 64-bit system, `sizeof(nint)` is 8 bytes, so `stackalloc nint[5]` allocates 40 bytes on the stack. The only minor caveat is that `sizeof(nint)` requires an `unsafe` context since the size isn't fixed at compile time (it's platform-dependent).
